---
description: Set QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen before any headless QApplication (pytest, python -c, scripts)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Running tests

This project has PySide6 UI tests via `pytest-qt`. Without a Qt platform, `QApplication` aborts the whole pytest process (signal 6 / ABRT), which looks like a mysterious crash — not a normal test failure.

`tests/conftest.py` sets `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen` by default. Prefer:

```bash
.venv/bin/pytest tests/ -q --tb=short
```

If you override env or see Qt platform / ABRT / coredump on pytest, explicitly set:

```bash
QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen .venv/bin/pytest tests/ -q --tb=short
```

Do not treat a Qt abort as an application logic failure until the suite actually reports pass/fail under `offscreen`.

# Headless QApplication

Any `python -c`, script, or pytest that creates a `QApplication` must set `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen` before the application is constructed. Qt aborts in `createPlatformIntegration` (signal 6 / ABRT and a coredump) when no platform is available — that happens before later calls such as `setHtml` or `setMarkdown`.

```bash
QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen .venv/bin/python -c '...'
```

```python
import os

os.environ.setdefault("QT_QPA_PLATFORM", "offscreen")
app = QApplication([])
```

`tests/conftest.py`, the CLI, and `ensure_qt_app` already set `offscreen` when the variable is empty. Do not change the GUI window launch (`run` / `_application` in `main.py`): the real window keeps the normal platform and must not force `offscreen`.
